    "architecture_impact": "diagram_change",
    "impact_reason": "The reviewed integrated repair implementation adds seven source-linked Function nodes and nine Code relationships for scoped admission, live-owner inspection, durable wakeup, original-review publication and independent verification. This review adds three component relationships exposing Epic-to-Workspace scheduling, Boss-to-Watchdog postcheck and Watchdog-to-Feature receipt persistence in both supervisor/team views. Root and child designs describe retained ownership, exact-generation state, failure and restart behavior; the postcheck requirement links inspectable tests. Context/container boundaries and existing stores remain unchanged. Final source-contract, bounded pinned rendering and seven actual context-to-Code/deep-link/pinned-source/Level-up journeys verify the committed model, with warm artifact reuse. Current plan 7b5e3881 and committed model/design are explicitly re-reviewed after the prior saved request was refused stale_revision; earlier requests and accepted snapshots are preserved. Final UI, normalized CI consumer and full repair journey acceptance remain assigned to Feature 4."
